source: crates/engram-cli/tests/cli/snapshot/help.rs
expression: "f.run_bare(& [\"link\", \"--help\"])"
---
$ engramdb link --help
exit: 0
--- stdout ---
Link two memories with a typed edge (or update an existing edge)

Kinds: contradicts, supersedes, supports, derived_from, related_to, duplicates. Symmetric kinds (contradicts, related_to, duplicates) are stored once and shown on both memories. Re-linking the same edge updates its confidence, note and status (e.g. `--status rejected`).

Usage: engramdb link [OPTIONS] <SRC> <KIND> <DST>

Arguments:
  <SRC>
          Source memory ID (supports prefix matching)

  <KIND>
          Edge kind

  <DST>
          Target memory ID (prefix matching within the same store; a full id for a target in another store)

Options:
      --store <STORE>
          The target's store, when it is not this one: `global`, `group:<name>`, or a project id

      --confidence <CONFIDENCE>
          How sure the link is, 0.0-1.0 (default 1.0)

      --note <NOTE>
          Why the two are linked

      --status <STATUS>
          Review status: proposed, confirmed (default) or rejected

      --winner <WINNER>
          Resolve a `contradicts` edge by direction: this memory (one of the two) supersedes the other, whose validity window closes. The edge is rewritten as `<winner> supersedes <loser>`

      --global
          Operate on the global (cross-project) memory store instead of the current project

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - pretty: Human-friendly colored output with formatting
          - json:   JSON output for programmatic parsing
          - plain:  Plain text output without colors

      --json
          Output as JSON

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-essential output

  -v, --verbose
          Verbose output

      --no-color
          No colored output

      --dir <DIR>
          Working directory (default: current directory)

      --embedding-backend <EMBEDDING_BACKEND>
          Embedding backend: auto, onnx, or ollama

      --in-process
          Force in-process model loading — never contact the shared embedding daemon. Equivalent to setting ENGRAMDB_IN_PROCESS=1

      --spawn-daemon
          Spawn the shared embedding daemon if it is not already running, then route through it. By default the CLI only uses a daemon that is already running (connect-only)

      --no-maintenance
          Skip the automatic main-worktree maintenance pass (orphan-project cleanup + a quick store health check) for this invocation. Equivalent to setting ENGRAMDB_DISABLE_AUTO_MAINTENANCE=1

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
